Subject: [PATCH 4/4] RISC-V: define_insn_and_split for multiply-add and
 bit-extract fusion.

Introduce RTL patterns for multiply-add fusion on RV32.

Also cheapen zero_extract / sign_extract in riscv_rtx_costs when
RISCV_FUSE_BFEXT_SRLI / RISCV_FUSE_BFEXT_SRAI is enabled.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/riscv/riscv.cc (riscv_rtx_costs): Cheapen zero_extract /
	sign_extract when BFEXT_SRLI / BFEXT_SRAI is enabled.
	* config/riscv/riscv.md (maddhisi4): Emit separate mul/add when
	RISCV_FUSE_MULT_ADD, not TARGET_XTHEADMAC, and not TARGET_64BIT.
	(umaddhisi4): New expand.
	(madd_fused): New insn_and_split.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/riscv/fusion-bfext-2.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/riscv/fusion-limm-condbr.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/riscv/fusion-madd.c: New test.

